## Handoff to the User

Phase 2 review stopped its automatic loop: Fix iteration 3 made no code changes, so another review round would repeat the same findings.

Before any other work, ask the user exactly one question with the ask-user tool described under Asking Questions. Use this question text verbatim:

> Phase 2 review needs your decision. Fix iteration 3 made no code changes, so another review round would repeat the same findings.
> 
> Open findings:
> - Craft: **High**: retry loop has no backoff.
> 
> Details: /state/feat-x/run-1/phase-02/implement/iteration-03/handoff/handoff.md
> 
> How should Phase 2 review proceed?

Offer exactly these options, with these labels:
- "Continue with guidance": the user types guidance as the answer; you apply it and Phase 2 review continues.
- "Accept and finish the phase": the open findings are accepted as they are and the phase passes.
- "Stop": Phase 2 review stops; the user resumes or rewinds the feature later.

If the answer is "Accept and finish the phase" or "Stop", make no changes and finish. Any other answer is the user's guidance: apply it as this round's fix, using the open findings as reviewer feedback where the guidance leaves something open, then finish. The harness records the answer in the decisions file.

Open findings and the previous fixer's note: /state/feat-x/run-1/phase-02/implement/iteration-03/handoff/handoff.md

## Approved Review Decisions

The user's review decisions for this phase: /state/feat-x/run-1/phase-02/implement/review-decisions.md

They override the phase plan's acceptance criteria and earlier reviewer findings where they conflict. Follow them, and leave a finding accepted as is alone.

